# Account API endpoint for the Worker. It powers accounts, friends, friend duels
# AND remote room battles — without it rooms only connect between tabs of the
# same browser, and the account UI says the service is not configured.
#
# On Vercel this goes in Project Settings → Environment Variables (it is inlined
# at build time), or in .env.local for local dev. Never commit a real URL here
# if the Worker is private, and never commit a secret - VITE_* ships in the bundle.
VITE_ACCOUNT_API=

# Google sign-in. The OAuth *client ID* of the web app you created in Google Cloud
# console. Public by design - it ships in every bundle that uses Google sign-in.
# The matching GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID secret must also be set on the Worker.
# See worker/README.md §Google sign-in.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Turnstile site key (public) for the register/login bot check. Optional: unset
# means the form never renders a widget and the API omits tsToken. The matching
# TURNSTILE_SECRET must be set on the Worker with `wrangler secret put` —
# an unset secret disables the check server-side, so dev and tests stay free of it.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE=

# Cloudflare Web Analytics (real-user metrics, free): create a site in
# Dashboard → Web Analytics, paste the JS-beacon token here. Unset means the
# beacon script is never injected — nothing leaves the page.
VITE_CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=
